            "userId": "smoke-local-test",
            "displayName": "Studio agent",
            "kind": "agent"
          },
          "body": "Fixed. The legal paragraph had its plain text sitting as bare JSX text nodes between the two coloured link spans, and Studio's renderer only kept the elements — so \"By clicking Agree…\", \", and\" and \"You can opt-out anytime.\" were all dropped. Each run is now its own `<span>` (`.legalRun` / `.link` / `.linkSpaced`) so every phrase is a real text node you can select and edit, and the word gaps between them are drawn with a `::after { content: ' '; white-space: pre }` rule rather than left as whitespace between JSX nodes.",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:33:17.426Z",
          "editedAt": null
        }
      ]
