        {
          "id": "fb9c9543-4d7d-442d-9653-fc7df836cbc0",
          "author": {
            "userId": "smoke-local-test",
            "displayName": "Studio agent",
            "kind": "agent"
          },
          "body": "Fixed. The wrapper was full width already; the button inside it was not, because I had written the rule as `.cta > :global(.btn)`. Studio's CSS-module compiler emits `:global(...)` verbatim into the injected stylesheet, which is not valid CSS, so the browser dropped the rule entirely. `Button` accepts a `className` and appends it to its own classes, so \"Agree\" and \"Maybe later\" now carry `className={styles.ctaButton}` with `width: 100%`, and `.cta` is a column flex container. Both buttons now measure the full 361px content width.",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:33:19.797Z",
          "editedAt": null
        }
      ]
    },
