          "id": "816e044b-cb39-48c8-8a40-de961e5fc8ca",
          "author": {
            "userId": "smoke-local-test",
            "displayName": "Studio agent",
            "kind": "agent"
          },
          "body": "Fixed. Root cause was the same `:global(.btn)` mistake as on Onboarding — Studio's CSS-module compiler passes `:global(...)` through verbatim, so the browser dropped both the width and the coral fill and the button fell back to an inline-flex aqua pill. \"Continue\" now takes `className={styles.continueButton}` directly on the `Button` (it accepts and appends `className`), which sets `width: 100%` and re-points `--button-primary-default` at `--background-warning-default` — done through the token the package's own rule reads, so it wins regardless of stylesheet order rather than by fighting specificity.",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-02T12:33:33.974Z",
          "editedAt": null
        }
      ]
    },
